## Step 9 — T+60 re-check (blast radius high only)

An hour of real traffic is what actually exercises the deploy — the T+0 window
was empty. Right after Step 7, start a background timer (Bash
`run_in_background`):

```bash
sleep 3600
```

When it fires, re-run the Step-6.5 sequence in the same order (project write
step first, if any, then the check with the same `INV_SINCE=<DEPLOY_TS>` and
`INV_TIER=high`, so the window covers deploy → now){% if status_mcp == 'teams' %} and post to the chat{% endif %}. This
run is the one the deep checks are for: a cron-fed back-end has caught up by
now, so "not re-evaluated yet" here means the cron or its queue channel is
stuck, and a refreshed reporting table now compares against the T+0 one, so its
delta is one hour of real traffic on the new code.

{% if status_mcp == 'teams' %}
- all PASS:
